<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/
../FrameXML/UI.xsd">
    <!-- type="AuraButton" template required to exist under this exact name
         for the 12.1 managed AuraContainer. Blizzard's internal
         Blizzard_AuraContainerFrameProviders.lua hardcodes an implicit
         inherit of a template literally named "CustomAuraButtonTemplate" for
         every AuraButton it creates, but Blizzard never shipped that
         template (it was only ever a placeholder name in their blog post).
         Container button creation fails with "Couldn't find inherited node
         CustomAuraButtonTemplate" without this. Do not rename it.

         Deliberately EMPTY of Layers/Frames: XML <Layers> children do not
         attach to type="AuraButton" nodes on this build (confirmed by
         testing — a template with Icon/Cooldown/Count layers produced a
         button with zero regions). The real recipe, reverse-engineered from
         EllesmereUI's working implementation: every AuraButton region
         (Icon texture, Cooldown frame, stack/duration FontStrings) is
         created and registered entirely in Lua via AuraEngine.lua's
         AE.MakeInitializer, using SetIcon/SetDurationCooldown/
         SetApplicationCount/SetDurationText. This template only needs to
         exist by name — see AuraEngine.lua for the actual visuals. -->
    <Frame name="CustomAuraButtonTemplate" type="AuraButton" virtual="true"/>
</Ui>
